        <h3 class="font-display font-extrabold text-lg" style="color: var(--text-ink);">
          Mental Math Secrets: How to Calculate Percentages in Your Head
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-muted);">
          Calculating percentages in your head is surprisingly simple once you master these mental math shortcuts:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl border" style="background-color: var(--bg-surface-soft); border-color: var(--border-hairline);">
            <div class="font-bold text-sm mb-1 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">🔄 The Reversible Percentage Trick (X% of Y = Y% of X)</div>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-muted);">
              Because multiplication is commutative, <strong>X% of Y is identical to Y% of X</strong>. When a problem looks intimidating, flip it!
              <br /><span class="font-semibold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">Example:</span> What is 16% of 50? In your head, calculating 16% of 50 is tricky. Flip it to: <em>What is 50% of 16?</em> Half of 16 is <strong>8</strong>. Therefore, 16% of 50 is exactly 8!
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl border" style="background-color: var(--bg-surface-soft); border-color: var(--border-hairline);">
            <div class="font-bold text-sm mb-1 text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400">🎯 The 10% and 1% Building Block Method</div>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-muted);">
              Shift the decimal point to find key benchmarks:
              <br />• <strong>10%:</strong> Move the decimal 1 place left (10% of $180 = $18).
              <br />• <strong>1%:</strong> Move the decimal 2 places left (1% of $180 = $1.80).
              <br />• <strong>15% Tip:</strong> 10% ($18) + half of that for 5% ($9) = <strong>$27</strong>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

